{"book":19,"chapter":29,"context":{"chapter":29,"title":"The Voice of the LORD","summary":"A thunderstorm rolls in from the sea, shatters cedars and shakes the wilderness, and all of it is 'the voice of the LORD,' who sits enthroned as King and gives his people peace.","background":"Title: 'A Psalm of David.' A hymn. The storm moves from the Mediterranean over Lebanon and Sirion (Mount Hermon) and south to the wilderness of Kadesh. Many scholars note that Canaanites credited storms to Baal; this psalm gives all such power to the LORD. 'Flood' (v. 10) is the word used elsewhere only for Noah's flood.","customs":[],"watchFor":["'The voice of the LORD' rings out seven times.","The storm ends in a quiet blessing: 'peace' (v. 11)."],"connections":["Psalms 96:7-9","Deuteronomy 3:9","Genesis 7:17","Exodus 15:18"]},"verses":{"0":{"w":[["מִזְמוֹר","mizmor","H4210","HNcmsa","a psalm"],["לְדָוִד","ledavid","H1732","HR/Npm","of David"]]},"1":{"w":[["הָבוּ","havu","H3051","HVqv2mp","ascribe"],["לַיהוָה","layahweh","H3068","HR/Npt","to Yahweh"],["בְּנֵי","benei","H1121","HNcmpc","O sons of"],["אֵלִים","'elim","H410","HNcmpa","gods"],["הָבוּ","havu","H3051","HVqv2mp","ascribe"],["לַיהוָה","layahweh","H3068","HR/Npt","to Yahweh"],["כָּבוֹד","kavod","H3519","HNcmsa","glory"],["וָעֹז","va'oz","H5797","HC/Ncmsa","and strength"]],"x":[[19096007,19096009,18],[66005011,66005014,11],[24013016,24013018,10],[13016028,13016029,9],[19068031,19068034,9],[23060012,23060012,9],[19002010,19002012,4]],"xn":7},"2":{"w":[["הָבוּ","havu","H3051","HVqv2mp","ascribe"],["לַיהוָה","layahweh","H3068","HR/Npt","to Yahweh"],["כְּבוֹד","kevod","H3519","HNcmsc","[the] glory of"],["שְׁמוֹ","shemo","H8034","HNcmsc/Sp3ms","name his"],["הִשְׁתַּחֲווּ","hishtachavu","H7812","HVtv2mp","bow down"],["לַיהוָה","layahweh","H3068","HR/Npt","to Yahweh"],["בְּהַדְרַת","behadrat-","H1927","HR/Ncfsc","in adornment of"],["קֹדֶשׁ","kodesh","H6944","HNcmsa","holiness"]],"x":[[19096008,19096009,21],[13016028,13016029,17],[14020